---
source: crates/forgejo-core/src/error/render.rs
expression: "snap(ErrorKind::TokenRejected\n{\n    host: \"git.example.org\".into(), login: Some(\"perf3ct\".into()),\n    settings_url: \"https://git.example.org/user/settings/applications\".into(),\n}, c)"
---
error: git.example.org refused your token (HTTP 401)

  request:    GET /api/v1/user
  host:       git.example.org
  login:      perf3ct
  token from: the OS keyring, entry fjo:git.example.org

what to do:
  the token may be expired, revoked, or from another server.
  1. create a new token at https://git.example.org/user/settings/applications
  2. fjo auth login --host git.example.org
  note: replacing a token requires creating a new one.
